# Security audit

Invoke with `@security-audit`. Run the checks. Report pass or fail. This is a leak-and-hygiene gate before `git push`, not a pentest or `@review-security` (code review subagent). Skip any step whose files or tools are missing, and say what you skipped.

Project map: `.cursor/rules/project-map.mdc`.

**Dual goal:** block secrets and scratch paths; **do not** block or omit firmware assets the repo is meant to ship (`.bin`, `.espdl`, `.rar` under `firmware/`).

## 1. What would go to GitHub

```sh
git status -sb
git diff --cached --name-only
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref @{u} 2>/dev/null || true
```

If upstream exists:

```sh
git log --oneline @{u}..HEAD
git diff --name-only @{u}..HEAD
```

If there is no upstream, treat **all local commits not on origin** as the push set (`git log --oneline origin/HEAD..HEAD` when `origin` exists). If that also fails, scan the working tree and index only, and say the history window is unknown.

## 2. Paths that must not be in git

Fail if any of these are **tracked** (`git ls-files`) or **staged**.

- `notes/` (Obsidian vault; read-only for agents)
- `temp/` (scratch)
- `teaching/` (local teaching workspace)
- `.venv/`
- `.cursor/skills/handoff/sessions/`
- `.cursor/plans/`
- `.env`, `.env.*` except `.env.example`
- `credentials*.md`, `credentials.json`, `secrets.*`
- `*.pem`, `*.p12`, `*.key`, `id_rsa`, `id_ed25519`
- `otp.bin` (Tuya key-tool output; not a factory flash image)

**Not forbidden:** product firmware under `firmware/`, including `*.bin`, `*.espdl`, `*.rar`, plug `factory-*.bin`, and `uart-debug/uart-capture/`. These are intentional repo artifacts for backup, restore, models, and UART bring-up docs.

## 3. Firmware assets that belong in GitHub

When this repo ships plug backup, camera stock images, or bundled models, those blobs **should** be tracked and included in the push set.

**Expected trees** (from `project-map.mdc`):

| Path | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| `firmware/SAD00006D-ai-cam/factory-firmware/**` | Stock Elecrow `.bin`, vendor `.rar`, flash guide images |
| `firmware/SAD00006D-ai-cam/yolo11n-detect/components/vespa_detect/models/s3/*.espdl` | Bundled INT8 models |
| `firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/factory-*.bin` | Plug rollback dumps (2 MiB) |
| `firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/backup.sh` | Plug read-only backup helper |
| `firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/uart-debug/**` | UART scripts, reports, `uart-capture/*.bin` and `.txt` |

**Completeness check:** untracked product blobs under `firmware/` (exclude ESP-IDF `build/` and already-tracked `managed_components/`):

```sh
git ls-files --others --exclude-standard firmware/ \
  | rg '\.(bin|espdl|rar)$' \
  | rg -v 'managed_components|/build/' || true
```

- If the list is non-empty: **fail** with *Untracked firmware assets. Stage with `git add` if they belong in this release.*
- List each path so the operator can add them before push.

**Docs/scripts without matching blobs:** if the push set touches plug backup or UART docs but no plug factory dump is tracked:

```sh
git diff --name-only @{u}..HEAD -- \
  'docs/3202087-lsc-plug/factory-backup.md' \
  'docs/3202087-lsc-plug/factory-firmware-pull.md' \
  'firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/backup.sh' \
  'firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/uart-debug/**' 2>/dev/null || true
```

When that output is non-empty, also run:

```sh
git ls-files 'firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/factory-*.bin' 'firmware/3202087-lsc-plug/uart-debug/uart-capture/*'
```

Fail if docs/scripts changed in the push set but the matching `factory-*.bin` or `uart-capture/` files are still untracked (use the completeness list above).

**Camera models:** if the push set changes `vespa_detect` or model picker code/docs, fail when any `models/s3/*.espdl` referenced in tree is untracked.

Do **not** fail merely because a `.bin` or `.espdl` is large or contains encrypted vendor data. Stock dumps may include Tuya partitions; that is expected for rollback images documented in `docs/3202087-lsc-plug/`.

## 4. Secret content (text only)

Scan **text** in the working tree. Skip binaries and third-party trees (product `.bin` / `.espdl` / `.rar` are not scanned here):

```sh
rg -i \
  --glob '!notes/**' \
  --glob '!temp/**' \
  --glob '!teaching/**' \
  --glob '!.venv/**' \
  --glob '!node_modules/**' \
  --glob '!firmware/**/managed_components/**' \
  --glob '!firmware/**/factory-firmware/**' \
  --glob '!firmware/**/*.bin' \
  --glob '!firmware/**/*.espdl' \
  --glob '!firmware/**/*.rar' \
  --glob '!**/*.pdf' \
  'BEGIN ([A-Z0-9]+ )?PRIVATE KEY|api[_-]?key\s*=|password\s*=|ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]|github_pat_|xox[baprs]-|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|sk_live_|AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]+' .
```

If upstream exists, also scan the unpushed text patch:

```sh
git diff @{u}..HEAD -- . ':!notes' ':!temp' ':!teaching' ':!.venv' ':!node_modules' \
  ':!firmware/**/managed_components/**' ':!firmware/**/factory-firmware/**' \
  ':!firmware/**/*.bin' ':!firmware/**/*.espdl' ':!firmware/**/*.rar' ':!**/*.pdf' \
  | rg -i 'BEGIN ([A-Z0-9]+ )?PRIVATE KEY|api[_-]?key\s*=|password\s*=|ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]|github_pat_|xox[baprs]-|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|sk_live_|AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]+'
```

If `notes/` exists and this push publishes the parent repo, also:

```sh
rg 'token=|sig=|SAS' notes/
```

If `gitleaks` or `trufflehog` is on PATH, run on the push set but **exclude** `firmware/**/*.bin`, `firmware/**/*.espdl`, `firmware/**/*.rar`. Do not install either for this command.

Hits in docs or examples: judge context. Fail on live-looking credentials. Example serial paths like `/dev/cu.usbserial-AG0KXO8J` in `docs/3202087-lsc-plug/factory-backup.md` are session placeholders; fail only when paired with real secrets.

## 5. Dependency audit

Python only for this repo.

- `.venv/` exists and `requirements/ltchiptool.txt` is present: run `.venv/bin/pip-audit -r requirements/ltchiptool.txt`. Skip if no venv or `pip-audit` is missing (say skipped).
- No `package-lock.json`; skip Node audit.
- ESP-IDF and camera build deps are operator-installed outside git; skip unless a lockfile and matching audit CLI are already on PATH.

Critical findings: fail, or record an explicit accepted exception.

## 6. Project policy (no extra shell unless asked)

- **Must stay out of git:** `notes/`, `temp/`, `teaching/`, `.venv/`, handoff `sessions/`, `.cursor/plans/`, env files, key material, `otp.bin`.
- **Must go to GitHub when part of this release:** firmware blobs under the table in section 3 (`.bin`, `.espdl`, `.rar`), including plug dumps and UART captures tied to docs/scripts in the push set.
- **Submodule path to inspect when staged:** none (no submodules).
- **Local servers must bind `127.0.0.1`, not `0.0.0.0`:** N/A today (no in-repo servers).
- **Live secrets that stay out of git (names only):** operator `.env`; extracted Tuya keys from `otp.bin` workflows; personal cloud API tokens not needed for the offline camera path.

## Pass / fail

| Fail | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Forbidden path tracked or staged | Stop; do not push |
| Untracked `firmware/` `.bin` / `.espdl` / `.rar` (section 3) | Stage assets; then re-audit |
| Docs/scripts changed without matching tracked blobs | Stage missing blobs; then re-audit |
| Secret-like value in text tree or unpushed diff | Stop; do not push |
| `notes/` token/SAS hit when publishing | Stop |
| Critical dep audit, no accepted exception | Stop |

On **pass**, state: *Security audit passed this session.* Confirm whether firmware blobs in the push set were included or none were pending. This does not prove GitHub org settings or full history are clean.
